      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Any integer divided by an integer is an integer.\nIn particular, every integer has the same number of trailing zeros as it does of digits.\nFor example, both $780$ and $7800$ have $1$ trailing zero.\nHence, all integers have the same number, $1$, of trailing zeros.\nWe call $1$ the 1st-digit number and similarly, we call the $n^{\\text{th}}$-digit number $n$.",
